  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0161_f59581fa3cda.jpg\" style=\"width: 477px; height: 108px;\" /><br /><br />Ethene, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are gases.</p><p>So total moles of gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br />By <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;Farady<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> mole of gas produced<br /><br />So, by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;Farady <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math> mole gas produced<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#957;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0.0821</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>273</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8.96</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></p>"
